WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.788
Establishing Beth's school was a family affair.

2
00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:18.066
Father worked all day on the roof repairs while Jo and Mother took charge of the painting.

3
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:27.192
John, on the days he didn't work, came to help with the floors, and Meg provided the refreshments while her babies entertained all the workers.

4
00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:31.230
Mr. Laurence, of course, was in charge of the entire project.

5
00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:38.279
The transformation of the old house was amazing, as each day, the place looked fresher and improved.

6
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:44.335
"Does anyone need a drink?" Meg called, holding up an inviting glass of cold juice.

7
00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:50.606
"I think we all do," stated Mr. Laurence as he motioned for everyone to take a break.

8
00:00:50.607 --> 00:00:56.951
While the workers were satisfying their thirst, a carriage slowly pulled up at the house.

9
00:00:56.952 --> 00:01:03.544
A tall, sturdy young man got out, then held out his hand to a stylishly dressed young lady.

10
00:01:03.545 --> 00:01:13.626
She kissed the young man. Then, looking at the crowd in front of the house, she yelled, "Mother! Father! Meg! Jo! It's me!"

11
00:01:13.627 --> 00:01:19.017
"Amy?" Mother called, not sure she could believe her eyes.

12
00:01:19.018 --> 00:01:23.938
Then she ran to meet her youngest daughter. She hadn't seen her in a year.

13
00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:30.159
Amy, too, lifted her skirts, and forgetting her ladylike manners, ran to embrace her dear mother.

14
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.831
"I can't believe you're home!" cried Mother, showering Amy with hugs and kisses.

15
00:01:35.832 --> 00:01:41.646
"Laurie!" shouted Jo when she noticed him lingering awkwardly by the carriage.

16
00:01:41.647 --> 00:01:47.180
He lifted his head eagerly as he saw his best friend running toward him with outstretched arms.

17
00:01:47.181 --> 00:01:51.827
Giving her a big hug, Laurie said, "It's so good to see you, Jo."

18
00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:59.842
"I'm so happy to see you, Laurie," replied Jo, "even though your dashing clothes are now covered in paint."

19
00:01:59.843 --> 00:02:04.796
Laughing, he said, "I don't think my wife will object under the circumstances."

20
00:02:04.797 --> 00:02:07.865
"Your wife?" Jo asked, stunned.

21
00:02:07.866 --> 00:02:15.711
Amy walked over to Laurie and waited till the others had caught up before announcing, "We got married in Italy last week."

22
00:02:15.712 --> 00:02:23.138
For a moment, no one said a word until Jo, recovering from the shock first, congratulated them sincerely.

23
00:02:23.139 --> 00:02:28.429
"I'm so happy for you both!" she said, her voice choked with emotion.

24
00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:33.456
"Thank you, Jo," Amy said warmly as she looked deeply into her sister's eyes.

25
00:02:33.457 --> 00:02:42.831
"Not only do I have my sister back," said Jo, taking their hands, "but now I have a new brother. I'm so pleased."

26
00:02:42.832 --> 00:02:47.018
Soon everyone joined in congratulating the newly married couple,

27
00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:53.370
until Mr. Laurence decided to call it a day and invited everyone to his home to celebrate.

28
00:02:53.371 --> 00:02:59.623
While Amy rode back with Mother, Meg, and the babies, Laurie decided to walk back with Jo.

29
00:02:59.624 --> 00:03:05.776
"I have so much to say, but I don't know how," Laurie said to Jo.

30
00:03:05.777 --> 00:03:08.983
"Then you don't need to say it," Jo replied.

31
00:03:08.984 --> 00:03:13.824
"We mustn't be burdened by the past but look forward to what lies ahead."

32
00:03:13.825 --> 00:03:16.782
"I'll always love you, you know," said Laurie.

33
00:03:16.783 --> 00:03:20.232
"But it's a different love than the kind I feel for Amy."

34
00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:27.594
"And you will always be my dear boy, my best friend," said Jo. "I will always love you."

35
00:03:27.595 --> 00:03:33.907
Jo and Laurie found great peace knowing that despite the bumpy road, their friendship had survived.

36
00:03:33.908 --> 00:03:37.013
At the Laurences' a feast was under way.

37
00:03:37.014 --> 00:03:41.784
Mr. Laurence wanted to know why Laurie and Amy had gotten married so quickly.

38
00:03:41.785 --> 00:03:46.741
More importantly, he wondered why they chose to do so in Italy.

39
00:03:46.742 --> 00:03:52.662
"France would have been a more romantic location, I should think," Mr. Laurence said with regret.

40
00:03:52.663 --> 00:03:58.566
Jo watched Amy place her hand on Laurie's as he tried to answer his grandfather's questions.

41
00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:03.462
"What a lovely couple they make," Jo thought, and she truly meant it.

42
00:04:03.463 --> 00:04:08.190
Suddenly, the servant announced to Mr. Laurence, "We have a visitor, sir."

43
00:04:08.191 --> 00:04:15.072
"A visitor?" Mr. Laurence looked around. "We're not expecting someone else, are we?"

44
00:04:15.073 --> 00:04:19.524
"The gentleman says he is a friend of Miss Jo's," the servant continued.

45
00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:23.133
"A friend of mine?" Jo repeated as she stood up.

46
00:04:23.134 --> 00:04:28.286
"Then show him in, by all means," said Mr. Laurence.

47
00:04:28.287 --> 00:04:36.705
To Jo's complete surprise, the Professor walked in, holding his hat nervously in his hand but with his head held up with dignity.

48
00:04:36.706 --> 00:04:43.337
"Professor Bauer! Fritz!" Jo shouted, her voice giving away her delight in seeing him.

49
00:04:43.338 --> 00:04:48.989
"Oh, Miss Jo." His features softened as he recognized a familiar face.

50
00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:54.162
"I apologize for the unannounced visit but . . . it is a long story."

51
00:04:54.163 --> 00:04:57.663
"No need to explain," Jo said happily.

52
00:04:57.664 --> 00:05:02.568
"Everyone, this is Professor Friedrich Bauer, my dear friend from New York."

53
00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:09.348
No other words were necessary for once they heard who he was, the Professor was welcomed like a family member.

54
00:05:09.349 --> 00:05:15.613
Jo made space for him at the table and soon they were all laughing and talking like old friends.

55
00:05:15.614 --> 00:05:19.242
"Where are you staying, Professor?" asked Mr. Laurence.

56
00:05:19.243 --> 00:05:28.812
When the Professor named a local hotel in town, Mr. Laurence shook his head and said, "That won't do at all. You must be my guest here."

57
00:05:28.813 --> 00:05:34.894
Then he rang for his servant to collect the Professor's belongings and bring them to the mansion.

58
00:05:34.895 --> 00:05:40.693
Jo still could not believe how easily the Professor blended in with her family and friends,

59
00:05:40.694 --> 00:05:46.270
sitting at the same table and telling jokes and stories as if he had known them all his life.

60
00:05:46.271 --> 00:05:51.291
"Jo?" Mr. Laurence had to call twice to get her attention. "Jo?"

61
00:05:51.292 --> 00:05:55.833
"Oh, sorry," Jo said. "I didn't hear you."

62
00:05:55.834 --> 00:06:00.325
"Would you mind taking Professor Bauer to see the school tomorrow morning?

63
00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:05.483
I've formally asked him to become the headmaster but he hasn't given me his answer.

64
00:06:05.484 --> 00:06:10.509
Make sure you get it from him tomorrow," Mr. Laurence said with a wink.

65
00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:16.207
Smiling at him, Jo said she would be more than happy to do that.

66
00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:24.476
The next morning, true to her word, Jo escorted the Professor to the school site, asking him along the way about his life in New York.

67
00:06:24.477 --> 00:06:29.272
"Never mind me, Jo," he said. "I am more concerned about you.

68
00:06:29.273 --> 00:06:33.146
How are you coping with the loss of your dear sister?"

69
00:06:33.147 --> 00:06:39.988
As it always was with the Professor, Jo felt safe and secure showing him her deepest feelings.

70
00:06:39.989 --> 00:06:46.713
By the time they reached the school, the Professor had already offered his warm words of encouragement and hope to Jo.

71
00:06:46.714 --> 00:06:51.737
"Well, here we are," Jo said as she stepped back for him to view the school.

72
00:06:51.738 --> 00:06:56.853
"It doesn't look like much yet, but we hope to open it by the next school year."

73
00:06:56.854 --> 00:07:03.390
"It exceeds all my expectations," the Professor said, his eyes watering with emotion.

74
00:07:03.391 --> 00:07:12.095
"It will be smaller classes, but the school promises to look after the individual needs and talents of each student," Jo went on to explain.

75
00:07:12.096 --> 00:07:16.247
"As all good schools should," the Professor agreed.

76
00:07:16.248 --> 00:07:23.269
"As Mr. Laurence mentioned last night, he is eager for you to become the headmaster of the school," Jo said.

77
00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.852
"And you?" the Professor asked Jo.

78
00:07:25.853 --> 00:07:35.316
"I'm to be your assistant, organizing lessons, making sure the pupils are behaving, and mending socks," Jo said with a twinkle in her eye.

79
00:07:35.317 --> 00:07:40.833
"Then," the Professor said, puffing out his chest, "I will gladly accept."

80
00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:43.229
They shook hands wholeheartedly.

81
00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:48.621
"By the way, have you decided on a name for the school?" he asked.

82
00:07:48.622 --> 00:07:52.293
Jo nodded. "Yes," she said with a smile.

83
00:07:52.294 --> 00:07:57.585
"It's going to be called Buffalo Academy."
